2 -> the Knowledge (OKF) view opens as a flat wall of **249 nodes + ~500 edges in one 812×3338px SVG** inside a 660px scroll box — no start-collapsed grouping at all, while the When and How-SW views correctly apply the `>3` drill rule (5 phases / 5 components at top). A first-time reviewer sees ~20% of an undifferentiated graph and scrolls blind -> give the Knowledge view the same tiered treatment (collapse by OKF `type` — its 6 types are natural containers — or by spine section) so it opens at a legible density -> @owner\n- [MINOR] U4 -> container-block click behavior diverges between the two drill views: in How-SW every `.block[data-node]` (component/module/file/external) opens the detail panel on click/focus, but in the When drill only leaf `.block[data-wi]` work items do — clicking or focusing a phase/workstream/campaign container in When silently does nothing (its only affordance is double-click-to-descend) -> bind the same click/focus→detail to When container blocks (the drill already has titles/counts to show) so the same structure carries the same idiom -> @owner\n- [MINOR] U3 -> two different legend idioms coexist, both in the same When tab: the phase-accent legend is a `p.tierlegend` (.82rem text, .55rem square swatches, inline flow) while the status legend below it is a `div.legend` (.85rem text, .8rem swatches, flex layout with different gaps); the What/Knowledge/How-SW tabs use only the second -> converge on the one `div.legend` idiom for the phase-accent row -> @owner\n- [MINOR] U1 -> the HTML type scale is ad-hoc at the small end: near-duplicate sizes serve the same role across sections — caption/legend text at .82rem (`tierlegend`), .83rem (`.detail .meta`), and .85rem (`.legend`, `.asof`, `.top-sub`); micro-labels at .68rem (`.detail .badge`), .7rem (`.pflow .g`), .72rem (`.entry span`, loop caption), .75rem (`.tile span`, `.pflow .n`) — 21 distinct font-size declarations overall, against the SVG side which correctly shares `--nlabel`/`--nsub` -> co